  "term": "smoothed curve",
  "definition": "A smoothed curve is a fitted line used to show the overall pattern in data, making it easier to see whether a relationship changes in a nonlinear way rather than following a straight line. In the source, smoothed curve fitting was used to examine the pattern between one measured factor and disease risk and to identify a possible turning point.",
